Link wrote:
> Should wands of teleportation work 100% against the monsters on Astral
> (except Riders)?  It seems like it trivializes the end level of the
> game when I can literally teleport a big path around the Riders, and
> not have to deal with most of the scary monsters.

It may be trivial, but at least it's intentionally as it is. The first
time I reported here about Astral's triviality was in 1996, must have
been version 3.2(?), where it had been possible to teleport away even
the riders; at least this part has been changed in subsequent versions,
now you have to meet at least one rider (if you don't jump around them).

Whether teleporting away the other nasties makes Astral trivial... - I
don't want to judge; since I died two times there (Pestilence, Famine).

But typically, because there are no straight corridors there, you need
more than two zaps to open a path. Using a wand of teleportation is one
but not the only option to reduce the difficulty of Astral; other means
are conflict and jumping boots. Should we remove those options? I don't
think so.

Janis


